 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to designating the \"Atomic\nVeterans Memorial Bridge\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S7114",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7114-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §344-m, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7114\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating the \"Atomic\nVeterans Memorial Bridge\"\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo designate a pedestrian bridge on the Taconic State Parkway within the\nTown of Yorktown as the \"Atomic Veterans Memorial Bridge.\"\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection One: Amends the highway law to designate a pedestrian bridge\nacross the Taconic State Parkway in the Town of Yorktown as the \"Atomic\nand Nuclear Veterans Memorial Bridge.\"\n\nSection Two: Designates the commissioner of transportation to provide\ninstallation and maintenance of adequate signing for the bridge\n\nSection Three: This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nBetween 1945-1963 the United States conducted approximately 235 nuclear\ntests. During this time, at least 220,000 American service workers\nparticipated in these tests, or served in the United States military\nforces occupying Hiroshima and Nagasaki.\n\nThese atomic veterans may have been exposed to radiation during their\nservice, and due to their exposure may have developed cancer or other\nmedical conditions later in life. This legislation seeks to ensure their\ndedication and sacrifices are recognized by designating a heavily traf-\nficked overpass bridge in their honor to commemorate their service.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nA9988b of 2019-20\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nCost of Signage.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
